<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Irish unemployment rate 12.5 pct in August - CSO.</title>
<headline>Irish unemployment rate 12.5 pct in August - CSO.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1996-09-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ireland's unemployment rate was 12.5 percent in August compared with 12.6 percent in July, Central Statistics Office (CSO) data showed on Friday.  </p>
<p>August unemployment, as measured by the live register of those claiming unemployment benefits, fell to a seasonally adjusted 284,300 from 285,500 in July, the CSO said.</p>
<p>			   Unadjusted	    Adjusted</p>
<p> Latest		  287,598		 284,300</p>
<p> Previous		288,375		 285,500</p>
<p> Year-ago		281,100		 277,700</p>
<p>-- Dublin Newsroom +353 1 676 9779</p>
</text>
